WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:01.846
- Welcome to Mom versus Chef. (in unison)

00:00:01.846 --> 00:00:03.476
- [Voiceover] A cooking competition where

00:00:03.476 --> 00:00:05.399
a professional chef and
a mom cook head to head

00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:07.390
preparing the best dish possible

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.183
with one secret ingredient.

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:15.049
Our first competitor
today is Sharzad Kiadeh.

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:16.451
- Hi, I'm Sharzad Kiadeh.

00:00:16.451 --> 00:00:18.646
I'm a mom, my son is one and a half

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:20.372
and his name is Adrice.

00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:22.262
I make YouTube videos, yay.

00:00:22.262 --> 00:00:23.786
I have a blog and a YouTube channel

00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:26.021
and I host a couple
different shows online.

00:00:26.021 --> 00:00:27.788
I've been experimenting in the kitchen

00:00:27.788 --> 00:00:29.535
since as long as I can remember.

00:00:29.535 --> 00:00:30.734
I'm not a professional,

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.644
I have no training whatsoever.

00:00:32.644 --> 00:00:34.433
I feel like my mom taught
me everything I know

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.525
and everything else I
learned from like blogs

00:00:36.525 --> 00:00:38.253
and watching other YouTube videos.

00:00:38.253 --> 00:00:40.894
Cooking for a small child
is obviously very different

00:00:40.894 --> 00:00:43.982
than cooking for my husband,
or my friends and family.

00:00:43.982 --> 00:00:46.258
Winning Mom versus Chef would be

00:00:46.258 --> 00:00:47.680
a dream come true.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.568
Uh no, it would be awesome bragging rights

00:00:49.568 --> 00:00:52.454
and I feel like it would make
my mom like really proud.

00:00:52.454 --> 00:00:54.283
I would give her all the credit.

00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:56.822
- And competing against her
is Chef Nyesha Arrington.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:59.078
- My name is Chef Nyesha Arrington.

00:00:59.078 --> 00:01:02.307
I have a restaurant called
Leona in Venice, California.

00:01:02.307 --> 00:01:04.189
We offer a cuisine that's called

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:05.519
progressive Californian cuisine.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.199
Cooking is one of those
things that found me.

00:01:08.199 --> 00:01:09.878
I grew up with my grandmother

00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:11.606
and would cook next to her

00:01:11.606 --> 00:01:14.693
and at a very young age I was able to

00:01:14.693 --> 00:01:16.684
understand what flavor was.

00:01:16.684 --> 00:01:18.127
Going into this competition, you know,

00:01:18.127 --> 00:01:19.997
I'm very excited.

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:22.576
I love love love kids.

00:01:22.576 --> 00:01:24.689
I hang out with my eight year old nephew

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:26.641
all the time, and we cook together

00:01:26.641 --> 00:01:28.163
and just winning Mom versus Chef

00:01:28.163 --> 00:01:29.566
would mean a lot to him.

00:01:29.566 --> 00:01:30.806
- Sharzad, Chef Nyesha,

00:01:30.806 --> 00:01:32.126
today you're gonna be competing to see

00:01:32.126 --> 00:01:34.056
who can make the tastiest dish possible

00:01:34.056 --> 00:01:35.681
featuring one secret ingredient.

00:01:35.681 --> 00:01:37.388
Let me introduce you
to our panel of judges.

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:40.070
- Hello, my name is Trent,
and I'm 10 years old.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.960
And I like playing outside with my friends

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:42.914
and on my skateboard.

00:01:42.914 --> 00:01:45.211
- Hello, my name is
Nathan, I'm 10 years old.

00:01:45.211 --> 00:01:48.401
And what I like to do for
fun is play video games.

00:01:48.401 --> 00:01:49.883
- And your last judge is me.

00:01:49.883 --> 00:01:50.757
My name's Andrew.

00:01:50.757 --> 00:01:52.261
I'm 25 years old.

00:01:52.261 --> 00:01:54.211
And I like reading outside.

00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:55.815
- And by the way,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:56.974
he is my twin.

00:01:56.974 --> 00:01:58.436
- And I'm not related to them.

00:01:58.436 --> 00:01:59.656
So I think it's time we find out

00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:00.996
what the secret ingredient is.

00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:02.358
Chefs, whatever you cook today will have

00:02:02.358 --> 00:02:03.821
to incorporate this ingredient.

00:02:03.821 --> 00:02:04.919
It will not be easy.

00:02:04.919 --> 00:02:05.852
Nathan, do you want to pull

00:02:05.852 --> 00:02:06.910
the top off this thing?

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.237
- Yes I do.

00:02:09.998 --> 00:02:11.583
Ohhh.

00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:12.355
- Beets.

00:02:12.355 --> 00:02:14.711
- Chefs, you're cooking with beets today.

00:02:14.711 --> 00:02:15.848
- So like, Beats by Dre?

00:02:15.848 --> 00:02:18.958
- This is more like beets by nature.

00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:20.583
- [Sharzad] I've never
cooked with them before.

00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.635
And I feel like most kids hate beets.

00:02:22.635 --> 00:02:24.342
- Chef Nyesha, what do
you think about beets?

00:02:24.342 --> 00:02:26.048
- I have cooked with beets in the past

00:02:26.048 --> 00:02:27.755
and have served them.

00:02:27.755 --> 00:02:29.746
- That smells like nature.

00:02:29.746 --> 00:02:31.351
- They smell really bad.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.549
- Guys, you're gonna have 30 minutes

00:02:32.549 --> 00:02:34.460
to prepare your dishes.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.557
Your time starts now.

00:02:35.557 --> 00:02:36.715
- Ahhh!

00:02:36.715 --> 00:02:38.381
- I think you can sneak a lot of veggies

00:02:38.381 --> 00:02:39.783
in a lot of kids foods.

00:02:39.783 --> 00:02:41.388
But beets?

00:02:41.388 --> 00:02:43.480
Bahhh. (laughs)

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.716
I'm gonna try and do something

00:02:45.716 --> 00:02:47.179
pizza related.

00:02:47.179 --> 00:02:49.576
So I see that there are some pitas

00:02:49.576 --> 00:02:51.710
and I'm thinking that
will be a good crust.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.152
Man down, man down.

00:02:53.152 --> 00:02:55.692
I see that there are jars of pesto.

00:02:55.692 --> 00:02:57.317
And cheese, of course.

00:02:57.317 --> 00:02:59.186
Those three things are like

00:02:59.186 --> 00:03:00.080
foolproof.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.056
- I'm running through the pantry

00:03:01.056 --> 00:03:02.153
I'm looking around I see

00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:03.819
the sweet potatoes.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:05.343
I see the beets.

00:03:05.343 --> 00:03:06.947
I see yogurt.

00:03:06.947 --> 00:03:08.756
Kids like hashbrowns.

00:03:08.756 --> 00:03:10.076
I'm gonna make a beet soda

00:03:10.076 --> 00:03:12.920
with a sweet potato and beet latke.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.139
- I take all my ingredients

00:03:14.139 --> 00:03:16.333
and then I just start
putting pesto on the pita.

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:18.753
And then I'm getting like
little slivers of beets

00:03:18.753 --> 00:03:21.840
that I'm just trying to place
all over the little pizza.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.790
I don't want it too beet-y.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:25.253
(laughs) Is that a word?

00:03:25.253 --> 00:03:27.935
- [Nyesha] I start to form
the mixture for my latke

00:03:27.935 --> 00:03:30.088
which is shredded raw beets,

00:03:30.088 --> 00:03:32.689
raw sweet potatoes, a little
bit of egg for a binder.

00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:36.021
And I start to form my patties

00:03:36.021 --> 00:03:37.565
get those crisping.

00:03:37.565 --> 00:03:40.471
I want the latke flavors to marry

00:03:40.471 --> 00:03:42.055
and really be delicious.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.457
- I'm going into this trying to like

00:03:43.457 --> 00:03:45.570
kind of mask the flavor of the beets.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.666
I dump a bunch of cheese on

00:03:47.666 --> 00:03:50.000
then I pop them in the oven for

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.544
10-ish minutes, or so.

00:03:51.544 --> 00:03:52.864
Now I'm just sort of

00:03:52.864 --> 00:03:55.282
waiting and hoping that it turns out okay.

00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:56.928
- So I'm grating my beets and I know

00:03:56.928 --> 00:03:59.366
that I want to sort of
squeeze all of the liquid out

00:03:59.366 --> 00:04:01.763
and I know I can use the
beet juice for the soda.

00:04:01.763 --> 00:04:03.368
So I add a little bit of lemon juice,

00:04:03.368 --> 00:04:04.608
a little bit of honey.

00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:08.601
I'm going to pour soda
water with the beet juice.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:11.394
- Chefs, there's only 15 minutes left.

00:04:11.394 --> 00:04:12.756
- You guys are half way there.

00:04:12.756 --> 00:04:13.670
- Ahhh!

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.174
- Whoa.

00:04:15.174 --> 00:04:16.555
- That's cool.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.973
- [Trent] She looks like she's
making like Kool-Aid, maybe.

00:04:18.973 --> 00:04:20.924
- So I make the first
beet cake and I kind of

00:04:20.924 --> 00:04:23.362
take a piece off and taste
it and it's delicious.

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.764
But I know I want more texture

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.430
so I say I'm gonna use the beet greens

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.177
and sort of crisp those up.

00:04:28.177 --> 00:04:30.757
- So of course I'm standing
next to Chef Nyesha

00:04:30.757 --> 00:04:33.845
and she's doing some magical sweet potato

00:04:33.845 --> 00:04:35.268
beet latke.

00:04:35.268 --> 00:04:37.604
And truly, I've never thought
beets looked appetizing

00:04:37.604 --> 00:04:39.453
until she steps in.

00:04:39.453 --> 00:04:41.586
And I was like, uh, I really want a bite.

00:04:41.586 --> 00:04:43.415
- Let's go see what the chefs are doing.

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:45.528
- Okay, you guys check on Chef Nyesha

00:04:45.528 --> 00:04:48.291
and I'll check on Chef Sharzad.

00:04:48.291 --> 00:04:49.063
- How's it going?

00:04:49.063 --> 00:04:49.815
- Pretty good.

00:04:49.815 --> 00:04:50.506
- Actually what is that.

00:04:50.506 --> 00:04:52.456
- This is a yogurt based sauce

00:04:52.456 --> 00:04:53.777
with a little bit of olive oil.

00:04:53.777 --> 00:04:55.565
It's basically going to

00:04:55.565 --> 00:04:59.202
counterbalance with the beet latkes.

00:04:59.202 --> 00:05:00.583
- That sounds delicious.
- [Nyesha] Right.

00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:01.538
- Thank you chef. (in unison)

00:05:01.538 --> 00:05:02.493
- Thank you judges.

00:05:02.493 --> 00:05:03.671
- Hello.
- Hi Andrew.

00:05:03.671 --> 00:05:04.545
- How's everything going?

00:05:04.545 --> 00:05:05.439
- It's going good.

00:05:05.439 --> 00:05:06.455
- This is one of the few times you've

00:05:06.455 --> 00:05:07.837
ever cooked with beets, is that right?

00:05:07.837 --> 00:05:09.117
- This is the first time ever

00:05:09.117 --> 00:05:10.173
that I've cooked with beets.

00:05:10.173 --> 00:05:12.367
- I tend to like when the

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.013
secret ingredient is showcased,

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.740
rather then let it be covered up.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.630
- I feel like that was like a subtle jab.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.767
- Oh no no no no no no.

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:19.804
I mean, we'll.

00:05:19.804 --> 00:05:20.515
- I'm a mom, I'm tough.

00:05:20.515 --> 00:05:21.938
- I don't know what it will turn out like.

00:05:21.938 --> 00:05:22.648
Well good luck.

00:05:22.648 --> 00:05:23.745
I can't wait to taste your dish.

00:05:23.745 --> 00:05:24.883
- Thank you, thank you judge.

00:05:24.883 --> 00:05:27.301
- Only five minutes left. (in unison)

00:05:27.301 --> 00:05:28.560
- [Nyesha] You know I
really feel I have a vision

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.775
when I go through and I'm
picking my ingredients.

00:05:30.775 --> 00:05:32.400
So I decided to grab the yogurt

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.494
and I know I want to
fortify it with some flavor

00:05:34.494 --> 00:05:36.850
and add some olive oil to it.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.130
That's gonna go down on the plate

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.791
to sort of eat and round
out the latke itself.

00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:43.717
- Now it's time to grab
my pizzas from the oven.

00:05:43.717 --> 00:05:46.684
They don't look super fancy,
they look very kid friendly.

00:05:46.684 --> 00:05:49.447
I'm not nervous because our dishes

00:05:49.447 --> 00:05:51.072
couldn't be more different.

00:05:51.072 --> 00:05:53.165
Hers is like real deal fancy,

00:05:53.165 --> 00:05:56.050
like mine is like kid friendly food.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.143
- I'm very confident in my dish

00:05:58.143 --> 00:06:01.657
because I feel that it
offers beets in a new light

00:06:01.657 --> 00:06:03.242
and I'm hoping they enjoy it.

00:06:03.242 --> 00:06:06.046
- I decide to just sprinkle a teeny bit

00:06:06.046 --> 00:06:09.115
of goat cheese on top of the pizza.

00:06:09.115 --> 00:06:11.187
And that's it, I'm cutting these up.

00:06:11.187 --> 00:06:12.509
I can't taste any beets.

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:13.421
Makes me happy.

00:06:13.421 --> 00:06:15.068
It's delicious.

00:06:15.068 --> 00:06:18.095
- [Boys] Five, four, three,

00:06:18.095 --> 00:06:21.137
two, one.

00:06:21.137 --> 00:06:22.748
- [Andrew] That's it.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:23.764
Time's up.

00:06:23.764 --> 00:06:25.085
Stop doing what you're doing.

00:06:25.085 --> 00:06:26.851
- Sharzad, can you please
bring out the dish.

00:06:26.851 --> 00:06:28.234
- Yes.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:29.250
- Thank you.
- [Sharzad] There you go.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.347
It's a pesto pizza.

00:06:30.347 --> 00:06:32.236
I know you guys are 10 year old boys.

00:06:32.236 --> 00:06:33.821
I'm gonna go out on a limb

00:06:33.821 --> 00:06:35.812
and say that you probably like pizza.

00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:36.909
- I love pizza.

00:06:36.909 --> 00:06:37.905
- Right, okay.

00:06:37.905 --> 00:06:38.676
So yay.

00:06:38.676 --> 00:06:42.070
So it's just pita bread with
pesto, mozzarella cheese,

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.304
and the beets are right
on top of the pesto

00:06:44.304 --> 00:06:45.382
under the cheese.

00:06:45.382 --> 00:06:47.717
And then a tiny little bit of
goat cheese on top of there.

00:06:47.717 --> 00:06:49.608
So, dive in there kiddos,

00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:51.563
let me know what you think.

00:06:53.304 --> 00:06:55.214
- I can really taste the beets

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:56.880
which, they don't taste that bad.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:57.796
- Okay, good.

00:06:57.796 --> 00:06:59.624
- I'm not sure about
the pesto and the beets

00:06:59.624 --> 00:07:00.599
together though.
- Okay.

00:07:00.599 --> 00:07:03.240
- [Nathan] It's like a pizza mix

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.150
that nobody would ever come up with.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.451
- The goat cheese is just

00:07:06.451 --> 00:07:08.117
a little bit too much maybe.

00:07:08.117 --> 00:07:09.519
Yeah, it's just not that good.

00:07:09.519 --> 00:07:10.413
- I don't know.

00:07:10.413 --> 00:07:11.651
It did taste very good

00:07:11.651 --> 00:07:12.871
and I think you did a great job.

00:07:12.871 --> 00:07:14.497
- Thank you for your honest feedback.

00:07:14.497 --> 00:07:15.512
- Thank you Sharzad.

00:07:15.512 --> 00:07:16.385
(laughs)
- You're welcome.

00:07:16.385 --> 00:07:17.096
- [Nathan] Thank you.

00:07:17.096 --> 00:07:18.965
Chef, can you describe the dish for us?

00:07:18.965 --> 00:07:21.303
- So, what I did was take the beet

00:07:21.303 --> 00:07:23.883
and use it in all of its formats.

00:07:23.883 --> 00:07:25.854
I sort of grated the beet raw

00:07:25.854 --> 00:07:27.438
and mixed it with sweet potato

00:07:27.438 --> 00:07:29.633
and cooked that together in a cake form.

00:07:29.633 --> 00:07:32.233
On the top is a crispy beet topped chip.

00:07:32.233 --> 00:07:34.813
And then to accompany that you have

00:07:34.813 --> 00:07:37.597
a beet juice infused soda

00:07:37.597 --> 00:07:39.100
that is sweetened with honey

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.543
and a touch of lemon juice.

00:07:40.543 --> 00:07:43.428
Just to kind of balance out
your entire beet experience.

00:07:43.428 --> 00:07:44.626
- Do you guys like how it tastes?

00:07:44.626 --> 00:07:46.455
- I actually don't really like this drink.

00:07:46.455 --> 00:07:48.263
When you put in the beets it just

00:07:48.263 --> 00:07:49.462
it just doesn't taste right.

00:07:49.462 --> 00:07:50.640
- [Nathan] I think it tastes good.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:51.859
- You definitely get the beet

00:07:51.859 --> 00:07:55.435
but it's not full frontal dirt water beet.

00:07:55.435 --> 00:07:56.508
- Right.
- [Andrew] I think it's

00:07:56.508 --> 00:07:58.835
like very refreshing.

00:08:00.271 --> 00:08:01.470
- That tasted really good.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:02.221
- What's that?

00:08:02.221 --> 00:08:03.603
- That tasted really good.

00:08:03.603 --> 00:08:05.045
- He said it tasted really good.

00:08:05.045 --> 00:08:05.878
(laughing)

00:08:05.878 --> 00:08:06.691
I don't know why we had to keep

00:08:06.691 --> 00:08:07.504
that a secret.

00:08:07.504 --> 00:08:08.703
(laughing)

00:08:08.703 --> 00:08:10.795
- I don't really like it.

00:08:10.795 --> 00:08:12.035
- I don't think I've ever had

00:08:12.035 --> 00:08:13.355
the beet leaf before.

00:08:13.355 --> 00:08:14.371
- Yeah.
- [Andrew] It's actually

00:08:14.371 --> 00:08:15.306
I don't know, it's cool.

00:08:15.306 --> 00:08:16.566
- This one's gonna be a tough one.

00:08:16.566 --> 00:08:17.907
(laughing)

00:08:17.907 --> 00:08:19.308
Thank you chefs for everything.

00:08:19.308 --> 00:08:21.970
- Give us a moment as
we discuss the winner.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:22.723
- [Sharzad] All right.

00:08:22.723 --> 00:08:23.636
- Thank you.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:25.221
- This is so weird, I've never really had

00:08:25.221 --> 00:08:28.085
anybody like, judge my food before.

00:08:28.085 --> 00:08:29.304
Yours looked amazing though,

00:08:29.304 --> 00:08:30.991
I just want to put that on record.

00:08:30.991 --> 00:08:32.027
Andrew was all about it.

00:08:32.027 --> 00:08:32.637
- [Nyesha] RIght.
(laughs)

00:08:32.637 --> 00:08:33.673
- Like he nailed your food.

00:08:33.673 --> 00:08:35.644
With mine, he was like.

00:08:35.644 --> 00:08:36.700
- Oh he liked it.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.021
- No I don't think he liked it.

00:08:38.021 --> 00:08:39.226
- They were good.

00:08:39.226 --> 00:08:40.479
- I'm really excited.

00:08:40.479 --> 00:08:42.104
And you did a killer job.

00:08:42.104 --> 00:08:42.816
- [Nyesha] You too.

00:08:42.816 --> 00:08:43.466
- Let's hug it out.

00:08:43.466 --> 00:08:44.238
Are we there yet?

00:08:44.238 --> 00:08:44.929
- Definitely.

00:08:44.929 --> 00:08:45.518
- Okay.

00:08:45.518 --> 00:08:46.148
(laughing)

00:08:46.148 --> 00:08:49.906
- So Sharzad made the
pesto pizza with beet.

00:08:49.906 --> 00:08:51.207
What did you guys think about that?

00:08:51.207 --> 00:08:52.710
- I just liked everything about

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.010
the pizza.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.367
And I liked how it was like something

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:57.993
that kids like.

00:08:57.993 --> 00:08:59.577
- But the goat cheese it was just

00:08:59.577 --> 00:09:00.857
too much goat cheese.

00:09:00.857 --> 00:09:02.645
- I kind of wish she had done something

00:09:02.645 --> 00:09:04.474
a little more with the beet.

00:09:04.474 --> 00:09:06.140
- What I did like about the chefs food

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.781
is that it actually tasted really good.

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:09.858
I hated the drink.

00:09:09.858 --> 00:09:12.520
- Her main dish, I did not really like.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.100
I felt like I tasted too much beet.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.400
- Yeah, I thought Chef Nyesha's dish

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.270
was really cool because it used

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.098
a lot of different parts of the beet.

00:09:20.098 --> 00:09:22.292
- I think we all know
who the winner is, right?

00:09:22.292 --> 00:09:23.796
- Okay, yeah, let's bring them back in.

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:25.645
- Chef Nyesha, Sharzad.

00:09:25.645 --> 00:09:27.087
Thank you for coming in today.

00:09:27.087 --> 00:09:28.388
It was a great competition,

00:09:28.388 --> 00:09:30.155
you both made some amazing dishes.

00:09:30.155 --> 00:09:32.451
Unfortunately, we can
only have one winner.

00:09:32.451 --> 00:09:34.828
- Sharzad, your dish was really tasty.

00:09:34.828 --> 00:09:37.084
- But Nyesha, we thought
your dish was tastier.

00:09:37.084 --> 00:09:38.221
- Wow.
- [Andrew] Congratulations.

00:09:38.221 --> 00:09:39.176
You're the winner of this episode.

00:09:39.176 --> 00:09:40.030
- [Nyesha] Oh my goodness.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:40.944
- [Andrew] Of Mom versus Chef.

00:09:40.944 --> 00:09:42.021
- [Nyesha] Oh my goodness.

00:09:42.021 --> 00:09:44.337
I am so excited I won.

00:09:44.337 --> 00:09:46.918
I wish little Emmanuel
was here next to me.

00:09:46.918 --> 00:09:50.229
Honestly, I feel very
honored to win this for him.

00:09:50.229 --> 00:09:51.387
- [Sharzad] I'm not that upset.

00:09:51.387 --> 00:09:53.988
Chef Nyesha's dish looked insane

00:09:53.988 --> 00:09:54.963
it looked amazing.

00:09:54.963 --> 00:09:57.035
But you know, there
can only be one winner.

00:09:57.035 --> 00:09:58.762
Sadly today was not my day.

00:09:58.762 --> 00:09:59.961
- [Andrew] Thank you both for coming in

00:09:59.961 --> 00:10:01.586
you both made some amazing dishes.

00:10:01.586 --> 00:10:03.827
This has been Mom versus Chef.

